Upstream's commit 48e1794414d338ce47abc0f27c25ade8788af9c3 (mtr's master
branch, 2026-06-16), which fixes CVE-2026-14461: ipinfo_lookup() in
ui/asn.c, which the AS lookups of -y and -z run, reads the reply to its
DNS query with the length res_query() returns, and that can be longer
than the PACKETSZ bytes of the buffer the reply is in, so it reads past
the end of the buffer. The length is clipped to the buffer's. mtr 0.96
does not hold the fix, and no release holds it.

From: R.E. Wolff <R.E.Wolff@BitWizard.nl>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 11:03:39 +0200
Subject: Fixed possible buffer overrun in asn code-- Michał Majchrowicz
---
 ui/asn.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ui/asn.c b/ui/asn.c
index 111c394..487d9e8 100644
--- a/ui/asn.c
+++ b/ui/asn.c
@@ -94,6 +94,8 @@ static char *ipinfo_lookup(
             DEB_syslog(LOG_INFO, "Malloc-txt: %s", UNKN);
         return xstrdup(UNKN);
     }
+    // Clip len to PACKETSZ. -- Michał Majchrowicz
+    if (len > PACKETSZ) len = PACKETSZ;
 
     pt = answer + sizeof(HEADER);
 
